{
  "source": "origin/main 5dc2ce9e mhseals_testing/agent_hook.py (literal hosts), test_hook_registry.CORPUS",
  "playbook": "RoboBoat playbook: you are boat agent claude-3f2a. Keep this id for the whole session (export BOAT_AGENT=claude-3f2a); every agent needs its own (a subagent too): the desk refuses a claim by an id that already holds one, and a claim works only with the id that made it. Ids are honour-based: never use another agent's --who.\nAct on the boat or its sim only through `~/astro_dock/src/mhseals_testing/tools/boat_agent <verb> --who claude-3f2a` (JSON out). On a boat host, ssh only to run boat_agent (claim, arm, run, start, reload, set, fcu, fence, ask, note, release, stop) or boat_tui; nothing else there. You may end your own tmux sessions there (name them `agent-claude-3f2a-...` and end them with `tmux kill-session -t agent-claude-3f2a-...`), never `boat`, another agent's session or `-L boat`.\n  1. `status`: what runs and who drives.\n  2. `claim --reason \"...\"`: ask the operator for the boat.\n  3. `run KEY` (`run mission --task NAME`) or `goal X Y [YAW]` with `--claim ID --dry-run`, then for real.\n     `arm --claim ID [--countdown S]` arms through the TUI: a banner counts down (agent.yaml arm.countdown, 5 s) and the operator may cancel it; the e-stop refuses it and arming never releases a hold. Sim only: `run KEY --sim-arm` arms a verified sim (its container sets MHSEALS_SIM_ARM=1) for that run and disarms after.\n     `run KEY --set K=V [--set K=V]` sets what the procedure measures before it starts (e.g. `run thrust_physics --set thrust_step=survey`); `set K=V --claim ID` sets any tunable key (the testing config schema; live Nav2 keys such as nav2.controller_server.FollowPath.vx_max too: mhseals_nav config/schema.yaml names them), within its range. While armed it refuses the keys reload.yaml marks armed-unsafe; never amplitude or command_mode while armed. The TUI shows and journals \"agent ID set K=V\". Exit 2: not_allowed (not tunable), bad_args (unknown key or value), busy (a procedure runs: never mid-segment), refused (armed-unsafe while armed).\n     `start COMPONENT --claim ID` / `stop COMPONENT --claim ID` starts or stops a stack part agent.yaml `start:` lists (odometry, EKFs, sensors, perception) as its TUI Status row does; its row shows your id; `reload COMPONENT --claim ID` respawns one. Never the driver, mux, Nav2 or watchdogs.\n     `reload config [NAME]` re-reads the TUI's YAML (hardware, settings, keymap, ...) as a hand edit does. `run f --claim ID` runs characterization (C applied live, read back).\n     `fcu get PARAM...` and `fcu rates` (IMU/odom rates, gap p99, FCU load, \"Main loop slow\") read only; `fcu set PARAM VALUE... --claim ID` (agent.yaml `fcu.set`: loop rate, SR0_/SR1_ stream rates, IMU filters; never yaw source, compass, servos, arming or failsafes), `fcu revert --to SNAPSHOT --claim ID` and `fcu restart --claim ID` (disarmed) go through the TUI's MAVROS link: snapshot, read-back and fcu_changes.md name you. SCHED_LOOP_RATE 400 only after `fcu rates` at 200 shows the FCU load low.\n     `fence corners LAT,LON LAT,LON LAT,LON ... --why \"...\"`, `fence on_exit alert|return --why \"...\"` and `fence anchor --why \"...\"` set fence_watchdog's course area at any time, no claim: validated, read back, kept in ~/.config/mhseals/fence.yaml and shown in the agent panel.\n     Start sims and heavy runs through the host guard: `.handoff/tools/heavy sim ...` (Unity headless).\n     No TUI (exit 4): `boat_tui up` (beside boat_agent) starts the stack and TUI in tmux and prints the line the operator attaches with; `boat_tui status` says who controls. Never type into its tmux session.\n  4. `follow --claim ID --until ...`: watch it.  5. `release --claim ID`: hand it back.\n  Every acting verb (claim, arm, run, goal, set, start, stop, reload, fcu set/restart, release) takes `--why \"...\"`: the TUI agent panel shows who, verb, why and result. `note --doing \"...\"` sets your \"doing:\" line there; `ask \"...\"` instead of guessing. `stop` any time: the operator and the agent it interrupts see your id; it cancels an arm countdown and keeps your claim (`release` it to claim again). `status` and `fcu get` work with no TUI controller.\n  `release HOLD --why \"...\"` (hold names in `status` .authority.record.holds) releases a lease or watchdog hold once its fault has cleared, at once; an operator hold (Space, stop, manual) only when ~/.config/mhseals/agent_grants.yaml grants it to you (then at once, e.g. a known bug the owner told you to clear). The e-stop is never releasable. When it is the best course of action and allowed, act yourself; say why.\nExit codes: 0 ok, 2 refused (read hint), 3 revoked or overridden (the hint says who: the operator or another agent; claim again only if asked), 4 no TUI (`unreachable`: the boat is off or out of reach), 5 agents blocked, 6 timeout, 7 paused by the operator.\nOperator state (`status` .operator; the operator sets it with S, manual control sets manual): `manual` (the operator drives) or `battery_swap`/`power_cycle` (the boat goes down; ETA in the hint): changing verbs exit 7 and your claim lease is suspended, not lapsed. Pause: no retry loop, one `follow --claim ID --until operator_state:state=normal` keeps the claim and returns on `normal`, then carry on (a claim not kept alive during the pause ends cleanly: claim again). Exit 4 with a down state or `unreachable`: the boat is down; check `status` every few minutes. When status shows `restarted_after`, re-check the stack, FCU params and RTK before anything else, and claim again (old claims are gone).\nNever publish /cmd_vel, /goal_pose, mux or MAVROS commands, change Nav2 lifecycles (params: `BOAT_AGENT_CLAIM=ID ros2 param set ...` or `set`), send raw test_pulses, start the mission runner or a procedure directly, never arm but through `arm`, release holds only with `release`: the hook blocks them and names the verb; kill only your own processes by exact PID; never answer a TUI popup. Run in sim first. For runs over 9 min use Bash run_in_background (the CLI keeps the lease). The TUI shows your boat commands: this machine's TUI; a boat session sets BOAT_AGENT_TARGET=blastoise-odroid in your environment (`blastoise` still works for one release; it means blastoise-odroid).",
  "brief": "RoboBoat workspace (drives a real boat). You are boat agent claude-3f2a. Act on the boat or its sim only through `~/astro_dock/src/mhseals_testing/tools/boat_agent <verb> --who claude-3f2a`; never publish /cmd_vel, /goal_pose, mux or MAVROS commands or kill its nodes yourself (the hook blocks those and names the verb). Before your first boat command read the playbook: `BOAT_AGENT=claude-3f2a python3 .agents/hook.py --playbook`. Repo-only work needs none of this.",
